            "review_title": "Review at Quan An My Hai",
            "review_text": "halfling17\nBeijing, China49 contributions\n0\nTasty Local Food\nJan 2020\nMy spouse and I ate a late dinner here the other night. We had walked by several times and always noticed a good customer presence. \n\nWe had roast chicken, spring rolls, and sauteed bok choy (or vegetable reminiscent thereof) with garlic. The roast chicken has tasty crisp skin and the meat was tender; it was served with a lime, chili, and garlic dipping sauce. The spring rolls were crispy and light, and the vegetable flavorful. \n\nThe restaurant appears to be a family endeavor and the service was cheerful and fast. A good option if you're hungry and in the area.\nRead more\nWritten January 23, 2020",
